## Testing ##
### User Testing ###
We had several of our friends participate in user testing to help identify any issues that we could then solve. They are listed below:
* Impossible apple issues - We initially had the apple being the same width/height as one segment of the snake. However, due to the use of accelerometer it can be very hard to peform two 90 degree turns in succession; there will usually be a one frame gap between them. For this reason, we made the apple have a width/height of two snake segments to make the apple easier to hit and thus make the game more enjoyable.
* Snake Movement - If you play any snake game online, you will realise that you are unable to turn in on yourself; if you are moving right, you can't turn left. Our game allowed this which obviously led to annoying instances where you would die in a seemingly random fashion. We fixed this by adding a check for the current move direction before allowing a direction change.

### Integration Testing ###
After developing each of the apps individually, we had to test the integrated system with the menu and also the introduction of the BlueTooth functionality to the snake game. The issues we identified were:
* Screen navigation issues - We found that when rendering the initial time display screen after the user presses a 'Back' button or 'Quit' after the snake game, it would usually flash the intended screen and then go straight to the menu. We fixed this by adding a very small delay after rendering the screen as we discovered the screen touch that triggered the render was still being registered afterwards.
* When printing the direction change to the BlueTooth serial monitor, we found that it was constantly printing 'changes' that were not changes at all. We fixed this by using a bool that ensured changes were only printed if they were actually changes.



## Self Assessment ## 
Overall, we think that we fulfilled our intial goal of demonstrating a bulk of the watch's capabilities. We worked well as a team and managed to create a functional product. We did attempt to have a more complex implementation of the bluetooth functionality by allowing the watch to connect to a phone and be able to skip, play/pause and go back to previous songs on the device's spotify. However, after trying extensively, we were running out of time and adapted our snake game to include bluetooth. If we had more time to dedicate to work on this project, we would revisit this idea and also develop more apps to display the watch's WiFi capabilities.
